  "summary": "This rich and comforting <b>Korean layered bake</b> offers a modern fusion twist on classic street food favorites by combining chewy rice cakes with savory protein. The star of the dish is thick-cut <b>smoked pork belly</b>, which provides a deep smoky flavor that permeates every layer during baking. Fermented kimchi adds a pleasant sharpness and crunch, balancing the richness of the meat and melt-in-your-mouth shredded mozzarella cheese topping. A signature sauce crafted from red pepper paste gochujang, garlic, toasted sesame oil, and clover honey coats the ingredients in a sweet and spicy glaze. Perfect for family dinners or game night gatherings, this casserole comes together with minimal effort and yields a piping hot, satisfying main course. The combination of chewy, crispy, and creamy textures makes it an instant crowd-pleaser that highlights the harmonious contrast between traditional Korean spices and hearty oven cooking.",
